From 4357278ad7e12b2a9024db76f1bf19d0a3cc4ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:26:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: Report charging current as
 positive

The battery manager firmware reports the battery current as negative
while charging. The power supply ABI wants positive values for charging
and negative values for discharging, and upower reports a battery whose
current_now is negative as discharging even when its status says
charging. On the Xiaomi 12T Pro the phone therefore showed
"discharging" on the charger, and at 2 % upower powered it off while it
was plugged in.

Negate the battery current read from the firmware.

Signed-off-by: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 84d9f9777..b7e6570ae 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1461,7 +1461,12 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_sm8350_callback(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 			battmgr->info.voltage_max = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
 			break;
 		case BATT_CURR_NOW:
-			battmgr->status.current_now = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+			/*
+			 * The firmware reports charging current as negative,
+			 * the ABI wants it positive (upower takes a negative
+			 * current as discharging, whatever the status says).
+			 */
+			battmgr->status.current_now = -(int)le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
 			break;
 		case BATT_TEMP:
 			val = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
-- 
